WEBVTT

1
00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:01.541
In verses 17.20 to 17.22 of Chapter 17,

2
00:01:01.541 --> 00:01:04.750
Lord Krishna explains the subject
of charity – daana.

3
00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.500
In the earlier verses

4
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.583
He described the three forms of austerity –

5
00:01:08.583 --> 00:01:10.166
bodily, of speech,

6
00:01:10.166 --> 00:01:12.416
and of the mind.

7
00:01:12.416 --> 00:01:13.583
He says –

8
00:01:13.583 --> 00:01:16.666
charity is not only a social duty;

9
00:01:16.666 --> 00:01:19.666
in Vedic culture it is considered an essential

10
00:01:19.666 --> 00:01:23.541
part of dharma and a means
of self-purification.

11
00:01:23.541 --> 00:01:25.333
But just as every action

12
00:01:25.333 --> 00:01:27.291
is influenced by the gunas,

13
00:01:27.291 --> 00:01:30.666
charity too can be of three kinds –

14
00:01:30.666 --> 00:01:34.083
sattvic, rajasic, or tamasic.

15
00:01:34.083 --> 00:01:36.166
This distinction is decided not by outer form,

16
00:01:36.166 --> 00:01:39.333
but by the feeling, consciousness,

17
00:01:39.333 --> 00:01:41.833
and purpose behind the charity.

18
00:01:41.833 --> 00:01:44.625
Why, how, and to whom it was given –

19
00:01:44.625 --> 00:01:47.625
this is what decides whether charity lifts the soul

20
00:01:47.625 --> 00:01:51.083
higher or places it in bondage.

21
00:01:55.875 --> 00:01:56.958
In verse 17.20,

22
00:01:56.958 --> 00:01:57.833
Lord Krishna

23
00:01:57.833 --> 00:02:00.583
describes the nature of sattvic charity.

24
00:02:00.583 --> 00:02:01.250
This charity

25
00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:04.083
is done with the feeling of datavyam iti –

26
00:02:04.083 --> 00:02:06.208
that is, ‘this ought to be done.’

27
00:02:06.208 --> 00:02:07.708
It is not driven by guilt

28
00:02:07.708 --> 00:02:08.333
or the

29
00:02:08.333 --> 00:02:10.958
expectation of some gain,

30
00:02:10.958 --> 00:02:12.291
but arises from a sense of duty

31
00:02:12.291 --> 00:02:15.416
and compassion.

32
00:02:15.416 --> 00:02:18.333
Such charity is anupakarine –

33
00:02:18.333 --> 00:02:20.250
meaning there is no hope

34
00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.583
of getting anything in return.

35
00:02:22.583 --> 00:02:25.500
The giver finds joy in the very act of giving,

36
00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.500
does not make a display of it,

37
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:30.583
nor waits for any reward.

38
00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:31.666
Sattvic charity

39
00:02:31.666 --> 00:02:34.958
is always deshe kale cha patre cha –

40
00:02:34.958 --> 00:02:36.375
which means

41
00:02:36.375 --> 00:02:37.500
giving to a worthy recipient,

42
00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.166
at the right time and the right place.

43
00:02:41.166 --> 00:02:42.333
For example,

44
00:02:42.333 --> 00:02:44.541
charity given on a sacred day like Ekadashi,

45
00:02:44.541 --> 00:02:46.958
at places of pilgrimage,

46
00:02:46.958 --> 00:02:49.958
or to such seekers and servants

47
00:02:49.958 --> 00:02:52.916
who are engaged in the upliftment of society –

48
00:02:52.916 --> 00:02:54.666
is considered to be

49
00:02:54.666 --> 00:02:57.708
of a very high order.

50
00:02:57.708 --> 00:02:59.416
Lord Krishna never forbids

51
00:02:59.416 --> 00:03:02.375
giving charity to the poor and destitute,

52
00:03:02.375 --> 00:03:06.250
but here He speaks of giving wisely.

53
00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:08.125
Charity given to a drunkard

54
00:03:08.125 --> 00:03:11.166
will only increase his bad habit.

55
00:03:11.166 --> 00:03:13.375
Rather than giving him food,

56
00:03:13.375 --> 00:03:15.375
it is better to give him good advice

57
00:03:15.375 --> 00:03:17.916
and connect him to some good occupation

58
00:03:17.916 --> 00:03:19.916
that becomes a means of living his life

59
00:03:19.916 --> 00:03:22.666
with dignity.

60
00:03:22.666 --> 00:03:23.916
Charity should be such

61
00:03:23.916 --> 00:03:26.958
that it truly uplifts the life of both the receiver

62
00:03:26.958 --> 00:03:30.083
and the giver.

63
00:03:30.083 --> 00:03:33.333
In the next verse, 17.21, Lord Krishna

64
00:03:33.333 --> 00:03:35.541
mentions rajasic charity.

65
00:03:35.541 --> 00:03:38.791
This charity is pratyupakararatham –

66
00:03:38.791 --> 00:03:40.166
that is, the giver

67
00:03:40.166 --> 00:03:45.208
hopes for benefit, prestige, or a
favour in return.

68
00:03:45.208 --> 00:03:48.833
Sometimes this charity is also pariklishtam –

69
00:03:48.833 --> 00:03:50.583
given unwillingly or under pressure,

70
00:03:50.583 --> 00:03:52.375
such as for showing off

71
00:03:52.375 --> 00:03:55.083
to people or to fulfil a social obligation.

72
00:03:55.083 --> 00:03:56.333
Many calculations

73
00:03:56.333 --> 00:03:59.625
of give-and-take are attached to this kind –

74
00:03:59.625 --> 00:04:00.791
‘Will I

75
00:04:00.791 --> 00:04:04.375
get a tax-saving benefit from this?’

76
00:04:04.375 --> 00:04:05.708
‘Will they invite me

77
00:04:05.708 --> 00:04:07.416
to the wedding?’

78
00:04:07.416 --> 00:04:08.875
or ‘What will people think

79
00:04:08.875 --> 00:04:11.208
if I do not give charity!’

80
00:04:11.208 --> 00:04:14.083
From the outside this charity may look grand,

81
00:04:14.083 --> 00:04:16.083
but the purpose behind it

82
00:04:16.083 --> 00:04:18.083
stains it.

83
00:04:18.083 --> 00:04:21.500
not a means of spiritual progress.

84
00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:23.583
In verse 17.22, Lord Krishna

85
00:04:23.583 --> 00:04:26.083
tells us about tamasic charity.

86
00:04:26.083 --> 00:04:29.875
It is given adesha-kale – that is,
at the wrong time

87
00:04:29.875 --> 00:04:32.041
or improper place.

88
00:04:32.041 --> 00:04:34.791
It is given apatrebhyah –

89
00:04:34.791 --> 00:04:37.500
to unworthy persons, such as a gambler

90
00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:38.791
or a criminal,

91
00:04:38.791 --> 00:04:42.500
or those who misuse generosity.

92
00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:44.583
And even if charity is given

93
00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:48.500
to the right person, but it
is asatkritam avajnatam –

94
00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:50.500
meaning given with contempt

95
00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:52.625
or insult –

96
00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:55.791
then such charity drags both down.

97
00:04:55.791 --> 00:04:58.125
Throwing a coin at a beggar

98
00:04:58.125 --> 00:05:00.458
comes under such charity,

99
00:05:00.458 --> 00:05:02.666
or forcing someone

100
00:05:02.666 --> 00:05:05.458
to beg again and again before
giving them charity –

101
00:05:05.458 --> 00:05:09.125
this too comes under tamasic charity.

102
00:05:09.125 --> 00:05:12.750
True charity is not merely the act
of giving an object.

103
00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:14.250
It is also connected to compassion,

104
00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:17.333
respect, and discernment.

105
00:05:17.333 --> 00:05:20.583
Charity is that which makes the giver humble

106
00:05:20.583 --> 00:05:24.708
and supports the receiver with dignity.

107
00:05:29.583 --> 00:05:34.125
Sattvic charity holds a quiet but

108
00:05:34.125 --> 00:05:36.583
deep power.

109
00:05:36.583 --> 00:05:40.750
When you give without any expectation –

110
00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:43.083
no praise, no return,

111
00:05:43.083 --> 00:05:46.166
not even thanks –

112
00:05:46.166 --> 00:05:49.500
then something within you changes.

113
00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:53.291
You become free of burden.

114
00:05:53.291 --> 00:05:57.416
Your heart becomes vast.

115
00:05:57.416 --> 00:06:00.458
And the one who receives it –

116
00:06:00.458 --> 00:06:04.333
feels not like an object of pity, nor indebted –

117
00:06:04.333 --> 00:06:08.958
but feels respected.

118
00:06:08.958 --> 00:06:12.625
This is sattvic charity.

119
00:06:12.625 --> 00:06:15.208
It neither makes noise, nor a display –

120
00:06:15.208 --> 00:06:19.541
yet it leaves behind a fragrance

121
00:06:19.541 --> 00:06:22.250
that lingers for a long time.

122
00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:25.125
Even a simple act –

123
00:06:25.125 --> 00:06:29.375
serving food, a few

124
00:06:29.375 --> 00:06:32.541
sweet words, or a small bit of help –

125
00:06:32.541 --> 00:06:36.166
can lift someone from within,

126
00:06:36.166 --> 00:06:41.458
if it carries sincerity and a selfless feeling.

127
00:06:41.458 --> 00:06:45.666
Slowly, without your even realising it,

128
00:06:45.666 --> 00:06:49.375
the ego begins to melt.

129
00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:52.375
You stop asking –

130
00:06:52.375 --> 00:06:55.708
‘Did they appreciate me?’

131
00:06:55.708 --> 00:06:58.375
And you begin to feel –

132
00:06:58.375 --> 00:07:04.083
‘I am grateful that I got the chance to give.’

133
00:07:04.083 --> 00:07:06.625
This very transformation is sacred.

134
00:07:06.625 --> 00:07:11.250
So the next time you give in charity,

135
00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:16.208
do not look at how large it is.

136
00:07:16.208 --> 00:07:18.416
Just consider

137
00:07:18.416 --> 00:07:22.333
how vast your heart is.

138
00:07:22.333 --> 00:07:27.500
This is where true purification begins –

139
00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:30.083
and this is where

140
00:07:30.083 --> 00:07:34.083
I quietly dwell.

141
00:07:38.833 --> 00:07:41.875
In family life, when charity

142
00:07:41.875 --> 00:07:44.958
is done with expectations –

143
00:07:44.958 --> 00:07:49.083
which I call rajasic charity –

144
00:07:49.083 --> 00:07:53.791
then it slowly begins to poison relationships.

145
00:07:53.791 --> 00:07:57.875
It is possible that you help a relative,

146
00:07:57.875 --> 00:08:00.083
bear the cost of someone's education,

147
00:08:00.083 --> 00:08:03.458
or give a large gift on a festival.

148
00:08:03.458 --> 00:08:08.291
But hidden behind all of this is a waiting –

149
00:08:08.291 --> 00:08:12.375
for praise, for respect, or for return.

150
00:08:12.375 --> 00:08:15.666
And when you do not get this,

151
00:08:15.666 --> 00:08:18.083
do you know what comes

152
00:08:18.083 --> 00:08:20.083
to the mind? –

153
00:08:20.083 --> 00:08:24.416
disappointment, bitterness, and complaints.

154
00:08:24.416 --> 00:08:28.708
Slowly, love turns into give-and-take.

155
00:08:28.708 --> 00:08:32.666
The giver feels they have been used,

156
00:08:32.666 --> 00:08:33.666
and the receiver

157
00:08:33.666 --> 00:08:34.958
feels they are

158
00:08:34.958 --> 00:08:38.583
being watched.

159
00:08:38.583 --> 00:08:42.416
Conversations begin to turn into transactions,

160
00:08:42.416 --> 00:08:45.375
and the warmth of family love

161
00:08:45.375 --> 00:08:46.875
begins to be lost.

162
00:08:46.875 --> 00:08:51.666
True charity does not keep accounts –

163
00:08:51.666 --> 00:08:57.875
it sets free. But when charity is
done only to be seen,

164
00:08:57.875 --> 00:08:58.833
to be praised,

165
00:08:58.833 --> 00:09:02.250
or in the hope of return,

166
00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:05.083
then even the greatest gift

167
00:09:05.083 --> 00:09:08.958
loses its dignity.

168
00:09:08.958 --> 00:09:13.083
I do not want your children to learn

169
00:09:13.083 --> 00:09:17.583
that every act of kindness comes
with a string attached.

170
00:09:17.583 --> 00:09:19.708
So give –

171
00:09:19.708 --> 00:09:24.083
yes, certainly give. But with respect,

172
00:09:24.083 --> 00:09:27.625
not by asserting authority. With affection,

173
00:09:27.625 --> 00:09:30.750
not by tying it to the bondage of conditions.

174
00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:32.791
In a family

175
00:09:32.791 --> 00:09:36.541
where generosity flows without any obstruction,

176
00:09:36.541 --> 00:09:40.958
there love deepens, ego melts,

177
00:09:40.958 --> 00:09:46.208
and harmony slowly returns.

178
00:09:46.208 --> 00:09:47.291
Reflect on this.

179
00:09:52.083 --> 00:09:54.291
Giving at the workplace

180
00:09:54.291 --> 00:09:57.875
is not always connected to money –

181
00:09:57.875 --> 00:10:02.750
it can also take the form of praise, recognition,

182
00:10:02.750 --> 00:10:07.625
or help given to a struggling colleague.

183
00:10:07.625 --> 00:10:10.750
But when this ‘help’ is given

184
00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:14.125
without respect, without discernment,

185
00:10:14.125 --> 00:10:18.375
or with a slight insult,

186
00:10:18.375 --> 00:10:22.458
then it becomes tamasic.

187
00:10:22.458 --> 00:10:23.583
Sometimes

188
00:10:23.583 --> 00:10:28.083
you announce your support publicly,

189
00:10:28.083 --> 00:10:32.333
only to embarrass the other person.

190
00:10:32.333 --> 00:10:33.375
Or you

191
00:10:33.375 --> 00:10:34.416
toss a benefit

192
00:10:34.416 --> 00:10:37.750
at someone in such a way

193
00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:41.583
that they begin to consider
themselves unworthy.

194
00:10:41.583 --> 00:10:44.583
If a poor employee is told

195
00:10:44.583 --> 00:10:47.333
that if he completes some very

196
00:10:47.333 --> 00:10:49.166
high-fee training,

197
00:10:49.166 --> 00:10:52.458
then his salary will be doubled –

198
00:10:52.458 --> 00:10:55.125
that poor man will only be left disheartened.

199
00:10:55.125 --> 00:10:58.291
This offer is a mockery of his poverty,

200
00:10:58.291 --> 00:11:01.458
and so it will be called tamasic.

201
00:11:01.458 --> 00:11:05.083
And it will become the cause of
the arrogant giver's downfall.

202
00:11:05.083 --> 00:11:06.458
Such ‘charity’

203
00:11:06.458 --> 00:11:10.666
in fact becomes a means of control.

204
00:11:10.666 --> 00:11:14.833
Its result may not show immediately, but slowly

205
00:11:14.833 --> 00:11:19.125
it has a bad effect on the work culture.

206
00:11:19.125 --> 00:11:22.208
People stop asking for help.

207
00:11:22.208 --> 00:11:25.750
They feel they are being judged,

208
00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:27.791
not supported.

209
00:11:27.791 --> 00:11:28.958
Remember –

210
00:11:28.958 --> 00:11:32.833
true support lifts up silently;

211
00:11:32.833 --> 00:11:36.458
false support slowly suppresses.

212
00:11:36.458 --> 00:11:38.750
Charity given with insult

213
00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:43.875
breaks trust. But that same small help –

214
00:11:43.875 --> 00:11:47.416
if given with dignity and humility –

215
00:11:47.416 --> 00:11:49.791
gives birth to loyalty, confidence,

216
00:11:49.791 --> 00:11:51.875
and unity.

217
00:11:51.875 --> 00:11:56.333
So before extending a hand to anyone,

218
00:11:56.333 --> 00:11:59.625
examine your heart well.

219
00:11:59.625 --> 00:12:01.875
If your support dims

220
00:12:01.875 --> 00:12:06.083
the light of someone's enthusiasm,

221
00:12:06.083 --> 00:12:09.708
then it is not support at all.

222
00:12:09.708 --> 00:12:12.750
Only when charity is done with a true heart

223
00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:16.666
and a selfless feeling does it become fruitful.

224
00:12:16.666 --> 00:12:17.583
Reflect on this.
